INFO 02-21 09:28:47 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-1585296a2a464991bb893603f39946a1-0: prompt: 'In both Microsoft Planner and Google Tasks, the team leader can easily notify a team member to ask for an update on a lead by using the commenting feature. Here\'s how:\n\nMethod 1: Using Microsoft Planner\n\n1. Open the Microsoft Planner plan for the project.\n2. Click on the task that the team member is responsible for and that you want an update on.\n3. In the task details pane on the right-hand side, click on the "Add a comment" field.\n4. Type your message asking for an update on the lead and press enter to send it.\n5. The team member will receive a notification about your comment and can respond with an update.\n\nMethod 2: Using Google Tasks\n\n1. Open the Google Tasks list for the project.\n2. Click on the task that the team member is responsible for and that you want an update on.\n3. In the task details pane on the right-hand side, click on the "Add a comment" field.\n4. Type your message asking for an update on the lead and press enter to send it.\n5. The team member will receive a notification about your comment and can respond with an update.\n\nIn both methods, the team leader can use the commenting feature to ask for an update on a specific task or lead. The team member will receive a notification about the comment and can respond with an update. This allows for easy communication and collaboration between team members, even when they are working remotely.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=13, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [128000, 644, 2225, 5210, 75865, 323, 5195, 47571, 11