INFO 02-21 09:28:48 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-9701a16ad1a541579f2162e0ec35e044-0: prompt: "Sure, here is an example Pygame code for an interactive display of a NOR gate:\n```python\nimport pygame\n\n# Initialize Pygame\npygame.init()\n\n# Set up the window dimensions\nWINDOW_WIDTH = 640\nWINDOW_HEIGHT = 480\nDISPLAY_SURFACE = pygame.display.set_mode((WINDOW_WIDTH, WINDOW_HEIGHT))\n\n# Define some colors\nBLACK = (0, 0, 0)\nWHITE = (255, 255, 255)\nGREEN = (0, 255, 0)\nRED = (255, 0, 0)\n\n# Set up the NOR gate\nNOR_IMAGE = pygame.image.load('nor.png')\nNOR_RECT = NOR_IMAGE.get_rect()\nNOR_RECT.centerx = WINDOW_WIDTH // 2\nNOR_RECT.centery = WINDOW_HEIGHT // 2\n\n# Set up the inputs\nINPUT_RADIUS = 20\nINPUT_POS = [(NOR_RECT.left - 50, NOR_RECT.centery - 50),\n             (NOR_RECT.left - 50, NOR_RECT.centery + 50)]\ninput_states = [False, False]\n\n# Define a function to draw the inputs\ndef draw_inputs():\n    for i, state in enumerate(input_states):\n        input_color = GREEN if state else RED\n        pygame.draw.circle(DISPLAY_SURFACE, input_color, INPUT_POS[i], INPUT_RADIUS)\n\n# Define a function to update the NOR gate output\ndef update_output():\n    if not input_states[0] and not input_states[1]:\n        pygame.draw.line(DISPLAY_SURFACE, RED, NOR_RECT.midright, (NOR_RECT.right + 50, NOR_RECT.centery), 3)\n    else:\n        pygame.draw.line(DISPLAY_SURFACE, GREEN, NOR_RECT.midright, (NOR_RECT.right + 50, NOR_RECT.centery), 3)\n\n# Main game loop\nrunning = True\nwhile running:\n    # Handle events\n    for event in pygame.event.get():\n        if event.type == pygame.QUIT:\n            running = False\n        elif event.type == pygame.MOUSEBUTTONDOWN:\n            # Check if an input was clicked\n            mouse_pos = pygame.mouse.get_pos()\n            for i, pos in enumerate(INPUT_POS):\n                if pygame.Rect(pos[0] - INPUT_RADIUS, pos[1] - INPUT_RADIUS, INPUT_RADIUS * 2, INPUT_RADIUS * 2).collidepoint(mouse_pos):\n                    input_states[i] = not input_states[i]\n    \n    # Clear the screen\n    DISPLAY_SURFACE.fill(WHITE)\n    \n    # Draw the NOR gate and inputs\n    DISPLAY_SURFACE.blit(NOR_IMAGE, NOR_RECT)\n    draw_inputs()\n    \n    # Update the output\n    update_output()\n    \n    # Update the display\n    pygame.display.update()\n\n# Quit Pygame\npygame.quit()\n```\nThis code creates a window with a NOR gate and two input circles. Clicking on an input circle toggles its state (green for false, red for true), and the output of the NOR gate is shown as a line that is red only if both inputs are false and green otherwise. You'll need to provide an image file named 'nor.png' in the same directory as the code to use as the NOR gate image.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=8, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [128000, 40914, 11, 1618, 374, 459, 3187, 5468, 5924, 2082, 369, 459, 21416, 3113, 315, 264, 70188, 18618, 512, 74694, 12958, 198, 475, 15041, 271, 2, 9185, 5468, 5924, 198, 52160, 8435, 2892, 2, 2638, 709, 279, 3321, 15696, 198, 41256, 14273, 284, 220, 14033, 198, 41256, 17807, 284, 220, 11738, 198, 69227, 92421, 284, 15041, 8344, 995, 7450, 1209, 41256, 14273, 11, 40359, 17807, 4489, 2, 19127, 1063, 8146, 198, 63949, 284, 320, 15, 11, 220, 15, 11, 220, 15, 340, 58099, 284, 320, 3192, 11, 220, 3192, 11, 220, 3192, 340, 57054, 284, 320, 15, 11, 220, 3192, 11, 220, 15, 340, 6641, 284, 320, 3192, 11, 220, 15, 11, 220, 15, 696, 2, 2638, 709, 279, 70188, 18618, 198, 45, 878, 19667, 284, 15041, 7502, 5214, 493, 45807, 3592, 1329, 45, 878, 70721, 284, 70188, 19667, 673, 17410, 746, 45, 878, 70721, 13729,