  2%|▏         | 1/50 [00:00<00:18,  2.66it/s]INFO 02-21 09:29:06 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-63f9ff0d7e784e7eb190781f99e41695-0: prompt: 'A single layer continuous perceptron network is a type of artificial neural network that can be used for linearly separable classification problems. This means that the input data can be separated into different classes using a single decision boundary that is a straight line. The decision boundary is determined by the weights of the connections between the input and output layers of the perceptron.\n\nFor example, imagine you have a dataset of flowers, with two features (petal width and length), and you want to train a single layer continuous perceptron network to classify the flowers into two classes (iris-setosa and iris-versicolor). The inputs to the perceptron would be the petal width and length of the flowers, and the output would be the predicted class of the flower. The perceptron would learn to classify the input data by adjusting the weights of the connections between the input and output layers. The decision boundary will be determined by the weights of the perceptron.\n\nIn summary, A single layer continuous perceptron network is a type of artificial neural network that can be used for linearly separable classification problems, which means that the input data can be separated into different classes using a single decision boundary that is a straight line. The decision boundary is determined by the weights of the connections between the input and output layers of the perceptron. Example: training a model to classify flowers into two classes using petal width and length as inputs.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=7, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_toke